course: dictionary
lesson: 6531
title: Words from a sports game
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Netball is a noun. It can name the game, as in «play netball», and it can name the ball, as in «a netball». When you see «netball» with no «a» in front of it, it usually means the game.
explain: The word is made of two smaller words you already know: net and ball. The net is the high ring with a net hanging from it, and players throw the ball through it to score. Knowing the parts of a word can help you guess its meaning.
explain: Read the words around netball to find clues. «But by month three Maddie misses two Saturdays because of netball» tells you netball is something you can miss on a weekend, like a game or a club. Check your guess by putting it into the sentence.
fact: Netball is a team game in which two teams of seven try to throw a ball through a high ring with a net.
fact: Netball is popular in the UK, Australia, New Zealand and other Commonwealth countries.
fact: A netball is the ball used in the game.
fact: In netball, players cannot run with the ball or dribble it; they must pass within three seconds.
exercise: «But by month three Maddie misses two Saturdays because of netball.» What is netball in this sentence? | A type of cake | *A team game played with a ball and a high ring | A kind of hat
exercise: In PE, the teacher throws «a netball» to Ruby. What is «a netball» here? | A high ring with a net | *The ball used in the game | A team of seven players | A bag for the kit
exercise: Which rule is true in netball? | You may run with the ball | *You must pass the ball within three seconds | You may dribble the ball down the court | You may hold the ball for as long as you like
test: «Ella is in the netball team at school.» What is a netball team? | A single player on the court | *A group of seven players who play together | A room where the kit is kept | A ball with a net around it
test: Players in netball wear a bib with letters such as GS, GA or GK on it. What does the bib show? | The score of the match | *The player's position on the court | The name of the school | The colour of the team's shirts
exam: What does a «netball bib» show? | Who won last week | *Your position in the team | The score of the match | Your age
